{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-160450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$\n- ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-160450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-154696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{1-x},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$\n- ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-154696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1$, we have $f(x)={e}^{1-x}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{1-x}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =0-(-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-154696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-154696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-154696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-154696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{1-2x},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$\n- ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=2{e}^{1-2x}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }2{e}^{1-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-2x}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-160455" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160455" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160455" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x/2},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$\n- ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\le 0,$ we have $f(x)={e}^{x/2}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{e}^{x/2}\\,{|}_{-\\infty }^{0} \\\\  & =2({e}^{0}-0) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-160447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 0,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(3x+1)^{3}}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-160459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-86917" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{-3x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-86917" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{-3x}$ on the interval $0\\le x<\\infty ,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }k{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }k{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x={[-\\frac{k}{3}{e}^{-3x}]}_{0}^{\\infty }=\\frac{k}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{3}=1\\,⟹\\,k=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-86917" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-86917" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-86917" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-86917" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{2-x},\\, & x\\ge -1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{2-x}$ on the interval $x\\ge -1,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }k{e}^{2-x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }k{e}^{2-x}\\,\\text{d}x=-k{e}^{2-x}\\,{|}_{-1}^{\\infty }=k{e}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\nk{e}^{3}=1\\,⟹\\,k={e}^{-3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-160469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{3}"] ["math" "3{e}^{-2}"] ["math" "e"] ["math" "{e}^{-3}"] ["math" "{e}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{1-2x},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{1-2x}$ on the interval $x\\ge 1,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }k{e}^{1-2x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }k{e}^{1-2x}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{k}{2}{e}^{1-2x}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty }=\\frac{k}{2e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{2e}=1\\,⟹\\,k=2e.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-160466" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160466" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2e"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2e}"] ["math" "e"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160466" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2e"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}},\\, & x\\ge -2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}}$ on the interval $x\\ge -2,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{k}{6(x+3)^{6}}\\,{|}_{-2}^{\\infty }=\\frac{k}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{6}=1\\,⟹\\,k=6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-160463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-160463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-87238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{-5x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-87238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{-5x}$ on the interval $0\\le x<\\infty ,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }k{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }k{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x={[-\\frac{k}{5}{e}^{-5x}]}_{0}^{\\infty }=\\frac{k}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{5}=1\\,⟹\\,k=5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-87238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-87238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-87238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-87238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-87219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X>6)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-3x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-87219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =P(6<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }3{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-3x}]}_{6}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-87219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-87219" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-87219" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{-1/2}"] ["math" "{e}^{-18}"] ["math" "{e}^{-3}"] ["math" "{e}^{-6}"] ["math" "{e}^{-9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-87219" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-18}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X\\ge 3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =P(3\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}x}]}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-126016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{e}^{-3}"] ["math" "{e}^{-1}"] ["math" "{e}^{-2}"] ["math" "{e}^{-3}"] ["math" "{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-86914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X\\ge 5)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}8{e}^{-8x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-86914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 5) & =P(5\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }8{e}^{-8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-8x}]}_{5}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-40}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-86914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-86914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-86914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{-16}"] ["math" "{e}^{-40}"] ["math" "{e}^{-5}"] ["math" "{e}^{-8/5}"] ["math" "{e}^{-8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-86914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-40}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X\\ge 2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2-2x},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & =P(2\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{2-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{2-2x}]}_{2}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-126032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{-2}"] ["math" "2{e}^{-4}"] ["math" "{e}^{-2}"] ["math" "{e}^{-3}"] ["math" "{e}^{-4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X>1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}0.1{e}^{-0.1x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1) & =P(1<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }0.1{e}^{-0.1x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-0.1x}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-0.1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a80aad35a5a3706c11e0922fd057bcc89fd105a1264e91ac7a0634cc9779403c"} {"question" "q-126018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-0.1}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{0.1}"] ["math" "{e}^{-0.1}"] ["math" "{e}^{-0.3}"] ["math" "{e}^{-2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "q-126018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-0.1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/state.json" "file_sha256" "977aa51b741d8ccc2546efb33829e56dfbad2c40d0dc50ce3da576bd32f4de4e"} {"question" "e-12329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/assets/d6ad9cbcf369609541984bb88a414653161a9ed723ec2637d6e73cc81b62a238.png)\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\geq 3$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\int_{3}^{\\infty} f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x = 1$\n\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/example-12329.json" "file_sha256" "9bd37b6cd60f83027b1a58d17854f45587a39e1ed4e8a3bad5c92031974eddb5"} {"question" "e-12329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\in S$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\int_{S} f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x \\geq 3,$ we have $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{(x-2)^2} \\geq 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }(x-2)^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x-2}\\,{|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/example-12329.json" "file_sha256" "9bd37b6cd60f83027b1a58d17854f45587a39e1ed4e8a3bad5c92031974eddb5"} {"question" "e-10851" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/assets/0ba485cc9b536bd1a7cd18f37c61d269515b2bcb621cabfa55d6a567d53144c6.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/example-10851.json" "file_sha256" "71801bb60613f239d4a1dba5f160f5d873a881ab2d17d3e748e0bbcb68a5d754"} {"question" "e-10851" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\in S$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\int_{S} f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x) = \\dfrac{k}{(4x+1)^3}$ on the interval $x \\geq 0,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\infty} \\dfrac{k}{(4x+1)^3} \\, \\textrm dx = 1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(4x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-{[\\frac{k}{8(4x+1)^{2}}]}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{8} = 1 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad k = 8.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/example-10851.json" "file_sha256" "71801bb60613f239d4a1dba5f160f5d873a881ab2d17d3e748e0bbcb68a5d754"} {"question" "e-10840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P\\left( X > 8 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/assets/cc8c2867f9ef99a8c476feeb319e03a3a479dd23f04e546bf1e5240daa4ea0ac.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/example-10840.json" "file_sha256" "6d6849cfb967d8b6201bad3024f7af4affa6dca9a0bd283b86a02f006197cfcb"} {"question" "e-10840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a <    X <    b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>8) & =P(8<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }5{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-5x}]}_{8}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-40}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/example-10840.json" "file_sha256" "6d6849cfb967d8b6201bad3024f7af4affa6dca9a0bd283b86a02f006197cfcb"}] "usage" {"e-10840" [] "e-10851" [] "q-86917" [] "q-86914" [] "e-12329" [] "q-154696" []} "basis" 2009 "retractions" [[17592186192966 :question/problem "$f(x) = {e^{1 - x},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $f(x) \\ge 0$ for all $x \\ge 1$\n2. $∫_{1}^{∞}f(x)dx = 1$\n3. $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function"] [17592186193218 :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$f(x) = {ke^{-3x},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$."] [17592186193217 :question/problem "Compute $P(X \\ge 5)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$f(x) = {8e^{-8x},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}x < 0$."] [17592186192355 :question/problem "${(1)/((x - 2)^{2}),\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 3, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\geq 3$\n2. $\\displaystyle \\int_{3}^{\\infty} f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x = 1$\n3. $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function"] [17592186192355 :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S$, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\in S$\n- $\\displaystyle \\int_{S} f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x \\geq 3$, we have $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{(x-2)^2} \\geq 0$.\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n$∫_{3}^{∞}f(x)dx|= ∫_{3}^{∞}(1)/((x - 2)^{2})dx; = ∫_{3}^{∞}(x - 2)^{-2}dx; =-\\frac{1}{x - 2} \\mid _{3}^{∞}; = - (0 - 1); = 1$.\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""] [17592186192301 :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n${(k)/((4x + 1)^{3}),\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$."] [17592186192301 :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\in S$\n- $\\displaystyle \\int_{S} f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 1$\n\nIn our case, for the function\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{k}{(4x+1)^3}\n$$\n\non the interval\n\n$$\nx \\geq 0\n$$\n\nthe second condition states that\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\infty} \\dfrac{k}{(4x+1)^3} \\, \\textrm dx = 1\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{∞}(k)/((4x + 1)^{3})dx &= - [(k)/(8(4x + 1)^{2})]_{0}^{∞} \\\\\n&= \\frac{k}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k$, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{8} = 1 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad k = 8\n$$"] [17592186192300 :question/problem "Compute $P\\left(X > 8 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n${5e^{-5x},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$."] [17592186192300 :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$, then\n\n$$\nP(a < X < b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X > 8) &= P(8 < X < ∞) \\\\\n&= ∫_{8}^{∞}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{8}^{∞}5e^{-5x}dx \\\\\n&= [- e^{-5x}]_{8}^{∞} \\\\\n&= e^{-40}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186190646 17592186190647 17592186190648 17592186190649 17592186190650 17592186192091 17592186192092 17592186192093 17592186192094 17592186192095 17592186192097 17592186192098 17592186192099 17592186192100 17592186192101] "immutable_fields" [[17592186190645 :answer-field/correct] [17592186190645 :answer-field/id] [17592186190645 :answer-field/key] [17592186190645 :answer-field/type] [17592186192090 :answer-field/correct] [17592186192090 :answer-field/id] [17592186192090 :answer-field/key] [17592186192090 :answer-field/type] [17592186192096 :answer-field/correct] [17592186192096 :answer-field/id] [17592186192096 :answer-field/key] [17592186192096 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
